.TH DOCUBROWSER 1 2026-09-13 "DocuBrowse 1.5.2" "DocuBrowse Manual"
.SH NAME
docubrowser \- local AI document search server and indexer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docubrowser
.RI [ lang ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docubrowser
is the command-line front end for DocuBrowse, a local, single-user
document search tool.
It scans a configured document directory, extracts and indexes text into a
SQLite FTS5 database, generates semantic embeddings and AI synopses through a
local Ollama instance, and serves a browser-based search interface on
.IR localhost .
.P
Everything runs on the local machine; no network connection, account, or API
key is required.
The server listens on port 8643 by default and binds to the loopback
interface only.
.P
An optional bare language code may appear in any argument position (for
example
.B docubrowser ko start
or
.BR "docubrowser start ja" ).
It sets the active interface and document language, is written to
.IR docubrowse.config ,
and persists for later runs.
Supported codes are
.BR en ,
.BR ja ,
.BR ko ,
.BR zh ", and"
.BR zh\-hant .
See
.BR docubrowse.config (5).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start the search server, after verifying that Ollama is installed, running,
and has the models required by the active language (pulling them if needed).
.TP
.B stop
Stop the running server.
.TP
.B restart
Stop the server and start it again.
.TP
.B status
Show server status together with the document, embedding, and tag counts.
.TP
.B scan\fR [\fITYPE\fR ...]
Scan the configured document directories, index the documents, and generate
embeddings.
An optional list of type keywords (for example
.BR "pdf txt" )
restricts the scan to those formats.
.TP
.B rescan\fR [\fITYPE\fR ...]
Alias for
.BR scan ,
kept for backward compatibility.
.TP
.B scan\-file \-\-file \fIPATH\fR ...
Extract, index, and embed a single file.
Useful for retrying a file that previously failed and was blacklisted.
The path may contain spaces without quoting.
.TP
.B embed
Generate or refresh embeddings for documents that do not yet have them.
.TP
.B open
Open the DocuBrowse user interface in the default web browser.
.TP
.B purge
Scan the index for personally identifiable information (PII) and remove
matching documents.
Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to preview matches without changing anything.
.TP
.B ignore\fR {add|remove|list} [\fIDIR\fR]
Manage the directories excluded from scanning.
Adding a directory also purges any already-indexed documents beneath it.
.TP
.B report
Walk the document directory and print a file-type breakdown.
This makes no changes to the database.
.TP
.B duplist
List duplicate documents by exact SHA-256 hash.
Add
.B \-\-near\-dups
to also report near-duplicates by embedding similarity.
.TP
.B dupclean
Review and remove duplicate documents through an interactive terminal
interface.
.TP
.B scan\-missing
Classify every indexed path as present, missing, or unmounted, and delete the
rows for genuinely missing files.
Rows on unmounted filesystems are left untouched.
Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to report counts only.
.TP
.B stopall
Stop all running scans, embedding jobs, and the server.
.SH OPTIONS
These global options may be given before the command.
Individual commands accept a matching subset; run a command with no arguments
for its specific options.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Use the SQLite database at
.IR PATH ,
overriding the configured
.IR db_path .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Use
.I PORT
for the HTTP server, overriding the configured
.IR port .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read configuration from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
For
.B purge
and
.BR scan\-missing ,
report what would change without modifying the database.
.TP
.BI \-\-doc\-dir " DIR"
For scanning commands, index
.I DIR
instead of the configured document directories.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of parallel extraction workers to use while scanning.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-embed
Skip the embedding step during a scan.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B docubrowser
exits 0 on success and non-zero on error, for example when Ollama is
unavailable or no document directory has been configured.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LANG
Active language code, overriding the configured
.IR lang .
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_DOC_DIR
Primary document directory to index.
.TP
.BR DOCUBROWSE_DB ", " DOCUBROWSE_DB_PATH
Path to the SQLite database.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_PORT
HTTP server port.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_WORK_DIR
Working directory for runtime data.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Base URL of the Ollama API used for embeddings and synopses.
A bare
.I host:port
is accepted; the scheme defaults to
.IR http:// .
Also accepted as
.BR DOCUBROWSE_OLLAMA_HOST .
.PP
See
.BR docubrowse.config (5)
for the full list, including the trusted-network variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/docubrowse.config
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ./docubrowse.config
Per-directory configuration file, read when no system-wide file is present.
.TP
.I ~/.docubrowser/
Per-user runtime data directory used by a packaged installation.
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan and index the configured documents, then start the server:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
docubrowser rescan
docubrowser start
.EE
.in
.P
Start the server in Korean, listening on a non-default port:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
docubrowser ko start \-\-port 9000
.EE
.in
.P
Preview which documents a PII purge would remove:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
docubrowser purge \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.in
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docuback (1),
.BR docubrowse.config (5)
.P
Full documentation is installed under
.I /opt/docubrowser/EndUser_docs/
and is available in the project repository.
